1
00:00:00,068 --> 00:00:01,988
The Gradual Irrationality

2
00:00:01,988 --> 00:00:04,148
Reduction Program.

3
00:00:04,148 --> 00:00:05,768
We ended wars using this

4
00:00:05,768 --> 00:00:08,368
exact program four thousand, two

5
00:00:08,368 --> 00:00:10,788
hundred and ninety-seven years ago.

6
00:00:10,788 --> 00:00:13,028
Before that we'd been fighting for

7
00:00:13,028 --> 00:00:15,628
twelve thousand years, which now seems

8
00:00:15,628 --> 00:00:16,908
like quite a long time to

9
00:00:16,908 --> 00:00:19,628
do something nobody enjoyed.

10
00:00:19,668 --> 00:00:21,168
Your nations have been hitting each

11
00:00:21,168 --> 00:00:23,248
other for ten thousand years because

12
00:00:23,248 --> 00:00:25,888
the other one hit them last.

13
00:00:25,888 --> 00:00:26,788
This is the conflict

14
00:00:26,788 --> 00:00:29,868
resolution strategy of four-year-olds,

15
00:00:29,868 --> 00:00:32,128
except four-year-olds eventually get tired

16
00:00:32,128 --> 00:00:34,108
and take a nap.

17
00:00:34,388 --> 00:00:36,848
Your species invented naps and then

18
00:00:36,848 --> 00:00:40,308
refused to apply them to geopolitics.

19
00:00:40,808 --> 00:00:42,068
You can't just stop being

20
00:00:42,068 --> 00:00:43,868
illogical all at once.

21
00:00:43,988 --> 00:00:45,048
That would be like teaching a dog

22
00:00:45,048 --> 00:00:47,708
calculus before it learns to sit.

23
00:00:47,928 --> 00:00:49,628
So this manual shows you

24
00:00:49,628 --> 00:00:51,428
how to bribe humanity into

25
00:00:51,428 --> 00:00:54,948
being less irrational gradually:

26
00:00:54,948 --> 00:00:57,208
Year one: Move one percent of

27
00:00:57,208 --> 00:00:59,888
murder money to medicine money

28
00:00:59,888 --> 00:01:00,948
(baby steps).

29
00:01:01,268 --> 00:01:03,708
Year two: "Hey, we didn't die!

30
00:01:03,708 --> 00:01:05,628
Let's do two percent!".

31
00:01:05,668 --> 00:01:06,788
Year five:

32
00:01:06,888 --> 00:01:09,408
"Remember when we spent money on bombs?

33
00:01:09,408 --> 00:01:10,788
That was weird.".

34
00:01:10,788 --> 00:01:13,308
Year ten: "What's a war?".

35
00:01:13,308 --> 00:01:16,368
Year twenty: "We used to WHAT?!".

36
00:01:16,628 --> 00:01:17,928
It's like weaning a baby

37
00:01:17,928 --> 00:01:19,828
off eating paint chips.

38
00:01:19,828 --> 00:01:20,968
You can't just take away all

39
00:01:20,968 --> 00:01:22,348
the paint chips at once.

40
00:01:22,348 --> 00:01:23,628
They'll cry.

41
00:01:23,628 --> 00:01:24,968
You have to gradually replace

42
00:01:24,968 --> 00:01:26,448
paint chips with food

43
00:01:26,448 --> 00:01:28,267
until they forget paint chips

44
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:29,976
were ever an option.
